I'm trying to create a virtual volume control that acts as
a Line Playback Volume (or master, if you prefer). I modified
control_hw.c in order to intercept r/w operations on the
following controls:

PCM out volume
Monitor mixer
Virtual volume

On writes to PCM-out it has to write the values modified by vvol.
That's ok, but how can I make alsa-lib to not deliver the events
about PCM out when they are generated by a write to vvol ?
I also need to keep the settings of the virtual mixer and PCM
out controls somewhere and system-wide. Is it fine to add two
fake controls to store them ?


